## Why This Is Asked
Tests ability to wire basic observability across static web apps, serverless functions, and a database, a foundational skill for troubleshooting in Azure.

## Key Concepts
- Application Insights integration on SPA and Function
- Correlation IDs across SPA -> Function -> SQL
- Log Analytics queries to join telemetry and database logs
- End-to-end request tracing and basic dashboards

## Code Example
```javascript
// SPA instrumentation and correlationId
import { ApplicationInsights } from "@microsoft/applicationinsights-web";
const appInsights = new ApplicationInsights({ config: { instrumentationKey: "<ikey>" } });
appInsights.loadAppInsights();
const correlationId = crypto.randomUUID();
fetch("/api/feedback", {
  method: "POST",
  headers: { "X-Correlation-Id": correlationId, "Content-Type": "application/json" },
  body: JSON.stringify({ text, rating })
});
```

```csharp
// Function: read header and insert into SQL with correlationId
string corr = req.Headers["X-Correlation-Id"];
using (var cmd = new SqlCommand("INSERT INTO Feedback (Text, CorrId) VALUES (@t, @c)", conn)) {
  cmd.Parameters.AddWithValue("@t", text);
  cmd.Parameters.AddWithValue("@c", corr);
  cmd.ExecuteNonQuery();
}
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you verify the correlation path in Log Analytics?
- How would you handle missing correlation IDs in edge cases?

## Why This Is Asked

This question probes design of a DR-ready, region-aware SaaS data layer with strict data residency and per-tenant isolation, plus global routing.

## Key Concepts

- Cosmos DB multi-region writes
- Private Endpoints / Private Link
- Azure Front Door for global routing
- ADLS Gen2 with Private Endpoints
- Azure Policy and RBAC for residency and isolation
- DR testing with defined RPO/RTO

## Code Example

```javascript
// Example: fetch tenant data with partition key to ensure isolation
const { CosmosClient } = require('@azure/cosmos');
const client = new CosmosClient({ endpoint: COSMOS_ENDPOINT, key: COSMOS_KEY });
async function getTenantItems(tenantId) {
  const { resources } = await client.database('TenantDB').container('Events').items.query({
    query: 'SELECT * FROM c WHERE c.tenantId = @tid',
    parameters: [{ name: '@tid', value: tenantId }]
  }).fetchAll();
  return resources;
}
```

## Follow-up Questions

- How would you validate DR plan coverage during an actual outage without impacting customers?
- What monitoring would you add to catch cross-region replication lag or schema drift?

